s7 = f'''<section id="limits" class="slide c-plum"><div class="sh">{SQ}<span class="mod">07</span><h2>Limitations &amp; Coverage</h2><p class="sub">What was and was not done</p></div>
<article class="task"><h3>Syllabus coverage</h3>{tbl(["Syllabus content", "Evidence", "Status"], cov)}</article>
<article class="task"><h3>Limitations (read before citing any number)</h3><ul class="lim">
<li><b>Data access:</b> the Google Drive folder could not be opened from the analysis environment. The four CSVs included in the public VIDA-NYU/LTS GitHub repository were used instead (shark_trophy, validation_sharks, data_leather, leather_validation). Any extra files only on Drive (e.g. the “animals” use case, images) were not analysed. Image columns were not used.</li>
<li><b>Labels:</b> “label” comes from the dataset authors’ labelling process for shark products; its quality was not independently audited. The dataset contains marketplace listings, not confirmed illegal trade.</li>
<li><b>Short time span:</b> shark listings were retrieved over ~10 days, and the time-series module uses crawl counts (a collection artefact) so it demonstrates technique rather than market behaviour.</li>
<li><b>Weak regression:</b> price is barely explained by title features (R² ≈ 7%) and is not usable as a price predictor.</li>
<li><b>Mixed currencies / data errors</b> in the leather file were identified but not repaired; USD is 99.98% of the shark file, so currency was ignored there.</li>
<li><b>Single random seeds and splits</b> (seed 42); small differences (e.g. SMOTE vs class weights) are within fold-to-fold variation.</li>
<li><b>Many tests were run</b> without multiplicity correction; with n ≈ 14.5k, p-values are almost always tiny, so effect sizes are emphasised.</li></ul></article>
<article class="task"><h3>Reproduce</h3><pre><code>pip install -r requirements.txt
git clone https://github.com/VIDA-NYU/LTS.git
DATA_DIR=LTS/data_use_cases python analysis.py   # writes results.json + figures/
python build_site.py                             # writes index.html</code></pre></article></section>'''

